{"id":"ba779aa7-d807-419a-83c0-22bc66556772","object":"chat.completion","created":1784992208,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Extract fields from case\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n\\n    # Build edges with mutual reachability weight\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        w = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        # Canonicalize: store as (min, max, weight)\\n        if u < v:\\n            edges.append((u, v, w))\\n        else:\\n            edges.append((v, u, w))\\n\\n    # Sort by (weight, node1, node2) for deterministic tie-breaking\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[2], x[0], x[1]))\\n\\n    # Kruskal's with union-find\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for u, v, w in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    # Check connectivity (if fewer edges than n-1, graph disconnected)\\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected')\\n\\n    return {\\n        'mst_edges': mst_edges,\\n        'total_weight': total_weight\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that takes payload (inner object) and returns a JSON object with mst_edges and total_weight. The payload contains nodes, core_distance dict, and distances list (each [node1, node2, distance]). Compute mutual reachability: max(core_distance[node1], core_distance[node2], distance). Build edges list with weight = mutual reachability. Then sort edges by (weight, node1, node2) where node1<node2 to canonicalize. Run Kruskal's algorithm using union-find to get MST. Return list of edges (each [node1, node2, weight]) sorted by weight then node1, node2? The output schema says prefixItems: [string, string, number]. The edges should be in some order. Typically we sort by weight then node1, node2 to be deterministic. Also total_weight sum of weights. Raise ValueError if graph not connected.\n\nWe need to ensure we don't modify case. Return dict with \"mst_edges\" and \"total_weight\". Use only standard library.\n\nImplementation code for solve(case). Then wrap in {\"implementation\": \"<escaped Python code>\"}.\n\nWrite code accordingly."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2017,"completion_tokens":765,"total_tokens":2782,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":247},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":97},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}